---
import DocsLayout from "../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";

const basePath = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, "");
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Terminal UI"
  description="Use the OpenTUI client: sessions, slash commands, themes, reviews, and keyboard shortcuts."
>
  <section class="doc-page">
    <p class="kicker">FIELD GUIDE / TUI</p>
    <h1>
      Drive Veasel
      <br />
      <em>from the terminal.</em>
    </h1>
    <p class="lede">
      The bundled OpenTUI client talks to the local loopback API. Sessions,
      reviews, and settings stay on your machine. Type <code>/help</code> in a
      session for the live shortcut list.
    </p>

    <div class="doc-panel">
      <h2>Home and sessions</h2>
      <ul class="guide-list">
        <li>
          <kbd>j</kbd> / <kbd>k</kbd> or arrows move the session list;{" "}
          <kbd>g</kbd> / <kbd>G</kbd> jump first/last when no filter is active;{" "}
          <kbd>1</kbd>–<kbd>9</kbd> open the Nth visible session (sidebar labels
          those slots); Enter opens; <kbd>n</kbd> starts a session when the list
          is empty.
        </li>
        <li>
          Type to filter by title or directory. <kbd>Ctrl+L</kbd> or Esc clears
          the filter; the status line states which match is focused. Home/End
          and PgUp/PgDn page long lists. Selection stays on screen with a plain{" "}
          <code>Selected N of M</code> cue.
        </li>
        <li>
          Esc cancels a running turn (it never clears the composer). Session
          history and events live in local SQLite.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="doc-panel">
      <h2>Composer and transcript</h2>
      <ul class="guide-list">
        <li>
          With an empty composer, <kbd>↑</kbd> / <kbd>↓</kbd> recall earlier
          submissions. PgUp/PgDn page the transcript; Home/End jump edges. End
          sticks to the latest reply while streaming.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Multiline drafts:</strong> <kbd>Enter</kbd> submits.{" "}
          <kbd>Shift+Enter</kbd>, <kbd>Ctrl+J</kbd>, <kbd>Ctrl+Enter</kbd>, or{" "}
          <kbd>Alt+Enter</kbd> insert a newline (OpenTUI <code>Textarea</code>).
        </li>
        <li>
          Readline edits: <kbd>Ctrl+A</kbd> / <kbd>Ctrl+E</kbd> ends,{" "}
          <kbd>Ctrl+←</kbd> / <kbd>Ctrl+→</kbd> or <kbd>Alt+B</kbd> /{" "}
          <kbd>Alt+F</kbd> by word, <kbd>Ctrl+U</kbd> clear draft,{" "}
          <kbd>Ctrl+W</kbd> or <kbd>Alt+Backspace</kbd> delete previous word,{" "}
          <kbd>Alt+D</kbd> delete forward through the next word,{" "}
          <kbd>Alt+C</kbd> capitalize the next word, <kbd>Ctrl+K</kbd> kill to
          end, <kbd>Ctrl+T</kbd> transpose characters around the cursor.
        </li>
        <li>
          <kbd>Ctrl+Y</kbd> copies the latest assistant reply (OSC 52). Esc
          dismisses a notice or review first; a second Esc returns home. Esc
          also cancels an in-flight turn — it never clears the composer.
        </li>
        <li>
          Transcript chrome tones fenced-code language tags, blockquotes, and
          muted diff context separately; add/remove diff lines use bold chrome.
          Truncated review summaries say how many lines remain (and{" "}
          <code>{"}"}</code> when more hunks exist).
        </li>
        <li>
          Status uses ● idle, ◌ busy, ▲ attention, and ✖ error. Idle shows the
          active provider/model when configured. Busy grows from{" "}
          <code>thinking…</code> to measured <code>streaming · N chars</code>.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="doc-panel">
      <h2>Credentials and models</h2>
      <ul class="guide-list">
        <li>
          <code>/connect</code> — paste an API key, save it locally, pick a
          model (happy path). Provider lists support the same j/k · g/G · 1–9 ·
          type-to-filter · Ctrl+L keys.
        </li>
        <li>
          <kbd>s</kbd> or <code>/models</code> — full settings: endpoint
          (Ctrl+U), output budget (Ctrl+O), and model discovery.
        </li>
        <li>
          Keys are stored under{" "}
          <code>$VEASEL_DATA_DIR/model-settings.json</code> with owner-only
          POSIX permissions (plaintext at rest). Saved profile keys win over
          environment variables for the same provider.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="doc-panel">
      <h2>Themes</h2>
      <p>
        Use <code>/theme</code> to switch among <code>mint</code>,{" "}
        <code>ember</code>, <code>slate</code>, <code>mono</code>, and{" "}
        <code>aurora</code>. The default mint theme matches the product mock
        (charcoal panels, mint accents, LOCAL cue).
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="doc-panel">
      <h2>Reviews and slash commands</h2>
      <p>
        Type <code>/</code> for suggestions. Common flows:
      </p>
      <pre><code>/patches
/patch show &lt;id&gt;
/patch approve &lt;id&gt;   # or reject

/commands
/command show &lt;id&gt;
/command approve &lt;id&gt;

/mcp add [user|project] stdio &lt;name&gt; &lt;command&gt; [args…]
/mcp add [user|project] http &lt;name&gt; &lt;url&gt;
/mcp enable|disable|remove [user|project] &lt;name&gt;
/mcp credentials
/mcp credential set|remove …
/mcp oauth authorize &lt;cred&gt; &lt;auth&gt; &lt;token&gt; &lt;client&gt; &lt;redirect&gt; [scope]
/mcp oauth complete &lt;cred&gt; &lt;callback_url|state code&gt;
/mcp trust configured/&lt;name&gt;
/mcp calls
/mcp call show &lt;id&gt;
/mcp call approve &lt;id&gt;

/skills [filter]
/skill on|off &lt;name&gt;
/plugin add|remove &lt;path&gt;
/map
/usage</code></pre>
      <p>
        File edits, shell, and MCP never take effect until you inspect and
        approve. After <code>/patch show</code> (or shell/MCP review) with an
        empty composer:
      </p>
      <ul class="guide-list">
        <li>
          <kbd>Space</kbd> multi-select · <kbd>a</kbd> / <kbd>x</kbd> approve or
          reject the selection (or current item)
        </li>
        <li>
          <kbd>Shift+A</kbd> / <kbd>Shift+X</kbd> approve or reject all pending
          of that kind
        </li>
        <li>
          <kbd>{"{"}</kbd> / <kbd>{"}"}</kbd> move between diff hunks ·{" "}
          <kbd>]</kbd> / <kbd>[</kbd> or <kbd>n</kbd> / <kbd>p</kbd> move
          between pending reviews
        </li>
        <li>
          <kbd>Ctrl+R</kbd> opens the first pending review list (patches,
          commands, or MCP calls)
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Configured MCP persists in user <code>mcp-servers.json</code> or project{" "}
        <code>.veasel/mcp-servers.json</code>; workspace <code>.mcp.json</code>{" "}
        imports read-only. Trust is still per-session. OAuth token values are
        never shown in the TUI — prefer headless{" "}
        <code>veasel mcp oauth … --listen</code> when Veasel should own the
        loopback listener (it still does not open a browser). See the{" "}
        <a href={`${basePath}/docs/mcp/`}>MCP guide</a>.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="doc-panel">
      <h2>Usage</h2>
      <p>
        <code>/usage</code> shows provider-reported token totals, average per
        reported turn, and optional cache counters when adapters set{" "}
        <code>usage.reported</code>. Veasel does not invent cost figures.
      </p>
    </div>

    <p class="doc-next">
      <a class="text-link" href={`${basePath}/docs/providers/`}>
        Configure providers <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
      </a>
      <a class="text-link" href={`${basePath}/docs/skills/`}>
        Skills and plugins <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
      </a>
      <a class="text-link" href={`${basePath}/docs/mcp/`}>
        MCP servers <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
      </a>
    </p>
  </section>
</DocsLayout>
